.TH REG 1 "2026-10-30" "Wunix" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
reg \- Windows NT Registry console tool for Wunix
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBreg\fR \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBreg\fR is a command-line tool for querying, adding, and updating keys and values in the Windows registry (HKLM, HKCU, HKCR) within Wunix.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBquery\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fB/v\fR \fIVALUE\fR]
Display key values or a specific value.
.TP
\fBadd\fR \fIKEY\fR \fB/v\fR \fIVALUE\fR \fB/t\fR \fITYPE\fR \fB/d\fR \fIDATA\fR
Add a new value or overwrite an existing value. Supported types: REG_SZ, REG_DWORD.
.TP
\fBimport\fR \fIFILENAME.REG\fR
Import keys and values from a Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00 text file.
.TP
\fBexport\fR \fIKEY\fR [\fIFILENAME.REG\fR]
Export a registry branch to .reg format.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
reg query "HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion"
.TP
reg add "HKCU\\Environment" /v MY_VAR /t REG_SZ /d "Hello"
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBuname\fR(1), \fBwsh\fR(1)
